 You can submit the file without an always-on server or a public port, and the upload instructions state no minimum GPU, processor or storage requirement and name no required third-party service.","The settings identified as live in pull request 315 admit up to six submissions per round and allow at most three hours, with 40 minutes for training and scoring ending by minute 170. The pull request proposes extending training to 60 minutes. The default-branch README describes a private test with a z-score threshold above 1, while the v2 code and settings identified in the pull request compare the current model and its challengers on the same draw of up to 2,000 public math problems. A challenger must complete the applicable draw, score enough tasks and pass the coverage and answer-length checks. At most one challenger wins, and it\u2019s the eligible challenger with the highest weighted gain if that gain exceeds 1e-12. The current model keeps a tie, and an earlier queue position breaks ties between challengers.","Up to ten distinct winning UIDs split the reward weight equally, provided their winning hotkeys remain registered on those UIDs. From round 98 onward, a decided round in which the current model holds removes the oldest winner until one remains, while a round without a decision leaves the paid set alone.","You can replace the file until the validator takes it, but a duplicate uses the hotkey\u2019s only counted turn and earns nothing, even if the validator catches it before training. Read from https://github.com/AffineFoundation/affine at commit e1e787a on 2026-11-23."],"how_it_was_made":"This note was put together by AI agents and not by a person who mines here. One agent read the subnet's public repository and wrote down what a miner does, what it takes and how the work is paid, with a source for each statement, and a second agent opened every source and took out whatever it did not support. Of 25 source checks, 13 held, 3 did not hold and 9 could not be opened, and only what held is in the text above. Nothing of the subnet's code was run, and the note describes the code as it stood on the day and at the commit named in its last sentence, so it can be out of date.","page":"https://check.loopholetape.com/mine/120.html"},"read_until":"2026-11-25T12:05:36Z","weeks":[{"entered_from":"2026-10-26","entered_to":"2026-10-28","entries":27,"wallets":22,"typical_fee_usd":183.3,"earning_after_7_days":0,"counted_at_7_days":27,"earning_after_14_days":0,"counted_at_14_days":27,"got_fee_back":4,"counted_for_fee_back":27,"typical_result_usd":-140.57},{"entered_from":"2026-10-28","entered_to":"2026-11-04","entries":75,"wallets":34,"typical_fee_usd":175.87,"earning_after_7_days":0,"counted_at_7_days":75,"earning_after_14_days":0,"counted_at_14_days":75,"got_fee_back":0,"counted_for_fee_back":75,"typical_result_usd":-166.65},{"entered_from":"2026-11-04","entered_to":"2026-11-11","entries":225,"wallets":41,"typical_fee_usd":135.04,"earning_after_7_days":0,"counted_at_7_days":225,"earning_after_14_days":70,"counted_at_14_days":225,"got_fee_back":4,"counted_for_fee_back":225,"typical_result_usd":-122.6},{"entered_from":"2026-11-11","entered_to":"2026-11-18","entries":184,"wallets":41,"typical_fee_usd":215.01,"earning_after_7_days":45,"counted_at_7_days":184,"earning_after_14_days":0,"counted_at_14_days":0,"got_fee_back":2,"counted_for_fee_back":64,"typical_result_usd":-200.27},{"entered_from":"2026-11-18","entered_to":"2026-11-25","entries":340,"wallets":43,"typical_fee_usd":155.49,"earning_after_7_days":0,"counted_at_7_days":0,"earning_after_14_days":0,"counted_at_14_days":0,"got_fee_back":0,"counted_for_fee_back":77,"typical_result_usd":-163.69}],"first_two_weeks_day_by_day":[{"day":1,"entries":327,"still_in":326,"paid_1_usd_a_day_or_more":4},{"day":2,"entries":327,"still_in":325,"paid_1_usd_a_day_or_more":1},{"day":3,"entries":327,"still_in":324,"paid_1_usd_a_day_or_more":0},{"day":4,"entries":327,"still_in":322,"paid_1_usd_a_day_or_more":